<!-- bpx-council:start -->
## bpx-council

`bpx-council` is an optional external advisor CLI. Use it for a user-requested
second opinion or a consequential decision, not after every turn. Council
stances share one backend unless routes are assigned; multiple seats can cost
multiple calls.

Ask a narrow question. Send only context the user explicitly selected for the
consult. Never gather files, run `git diff`, or forward secrets automatically.
Ask which paths or excerpt to share when context is needed. Pass the question
as one safely quoted argument, not raw shell interpolation. For no stdin
context, use `bpx-council --format json --no-stdin --question <quoted question>`.
Only use `--file <path>` for selected files, after checking for secrets.
`--isolate` does not promise CLI filesystem isolation.

Read versioned JSON receipt: `status` is `complete`, `partial`, or `failed`.
Partial advice can arrive with nonzero exit; report `error`, failed `attempts`,
and `notRun`, rather than dropping it. Missing or invalid receipt is failure.
CLI token usage may be unknown, not free. Treat verdict as advice, not proof.
<!-- bpx-council:end -->
